      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0072" n="art0072">
        <head>BIRTHS, MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</head>
        <p>BIRTHS, MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths. in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in the " Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, is. 6d. each; every additional seven words. 6d.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0073" n="art0073">
        <head>Deaths.</head>
        <p>Deaths.</p>
        <p>TITCHETT.—August 3rd, at 65, Ellesmere-street, John Henry Titchett, aged 29 years. BAMFORTH.—August 4th, at 74, Winwick-street,</p>
        <p>Joseph Bamforth-, aged GO years. CARRINGTON.—August sth, at 25, Leonard-street,</p>
        <p>)I.c,</p>
        <p>William Carrington, aged 57 years. TYSON.—August 6th, at 81, Forster-street, Minnie Tyson, aged '2l years.</p>
