      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0167" n="art0167">
        <head>INCIDENTS IN BOWLERS' WORLD.</head>
        <p>INCIDENTS IN BOWLERS' WORLD.</p>
        <p>WORKS' ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>Annual Handicap.</p>
        <p>This huge handicap commenced on Saturday and the following were the winners H. Fogg, LW; W. Holland, C &amp; J; H. Ather- ton, LW; J. Barnard, N; W. Birchall, C; H. Hughes, G; C. Perry, WR; E. Rowlands, CA; E. Barnes, Ry; G. Cook, WR; F. Burgess, WT; A. Holloway, LW; J. Keirman, AA; R. Barnett, P &amp; K; T. Clare, Ry; J. George, PP. Abbreviations: AA, Assurance Agents; AR, Artnitage and Rigby's; CJ, Carpenters and Joiners; CA, County Asylum; C, Crosfield's; CL, Cheshire Lines; F, Forshaw's;, FL, Flet- cher's; GT,Grappenhall Tannery; G, Greening's ; HT, Howley Tannery; LW, Longford Wire; L, LOcker's; L and N-W, Railway; MH, Monks, Hall; N, Naylor's; OT, Orford Tannery; PP, Plumbers and Painters; P &amp; K, Pearson and Knowles; By, tßylands; R, Richmond's SHF, Stockton Heath Forge; SHC, St. Helens Cable; TG, Thewlis and Griffiths; WR, Wire Ropery; WC, Warrington Corporation; WX, Whitecross; WT, Warrington Tannery; MWL, Mersey White Lead; WB, Walker's Brewery; WP, Warring- ton Printers; FM, Firth Mattress. The draw for next Saturday's games are as follows :</p>
        <p>_ 2.0. E. Warburton, C (5) v. T. Howard, CJ (6). J. Perry, CL (6) v. P. Wright, C (3). P. Jefferson, LW (7)-v. J. Booth, GT (6). J. Hankey, Ry (4) v. J. Lawless, FM (6). H. Smith, R (5) v. J. Feeney, P &amp; K (5). H. Wilson, WR (3), byei H. Wright, WX (4) v. J. Armitage, P &amp; K (4). J. Heywood, C (6) v. D. Robinson, C (5).</p>
        <p>2.25. M. Hayes, Ry (7) v. B. Regan, FL (3). F. Boscow, II (5) v. J. Sankey, P &amp; K (7). A. Foster, WX (7) v. H. Broadhurst, C (2). J. Meachin, MWL (4) v. B. Lowe, WX (6). H. Me Waters, WB (6) v. G. Stevens, P &amp; K (6) J. Wright, WP (6) v. J. Simcock, -CJ (5). W. Farrington, P &amp; K (4) v. W. Sutton, OT (7) A. Gleave, jun., C (3) v. J. Kenwright, FM (6).</p>
        <p>2.50 J. Monks, C (7) v. D. Ford, TO (7). B. Straw, 0 (3) v. G. Warburton, yy (6). T. Platt, By (3), bye. J. Warburton, R (7) v. E. Coyne, P &amp; K (3). H. Higham, PK (1) v. W. Butterworth, FM (3) G. Crozier, CL (5) v. C. Tranter, MH (5). G. Newell, CL (7) v. T. Garnett, CL (5). A. Payne, C (5) v. W. Robinson, HT (5).</p>
        <p>3.15. S. Taylor, C (5) v. W. Holmes (7). R. Torulinson, CL (s)\ v. H. Whitley, FL (4). J. Goulden, GT (7) v. J. Wilcox, FM (5). T. Pownall, G (7) v. H. Millman, P &amp; K (7). W. Holloway, LW (4) v. H. Eyes, Ry (ser.). W. Holden, Ry (7) v. J. Timmins, MH (4). W. Massey, R (7) v. H. Holbrook, AR (3). B. Jennings, C (5) v. W. Taylor, F (3).</p>
        <p>3.40. D. Melling, CJ (4), rbye. D. Jones, CA (4) v. J. Miller, C (6). J. Ashburner, C (5) v. W. Crawford, PK (3). E. Taylor, LN-W (4) v. T. Boyd, AA (4). P. Gleave, MH (7) v. J. Shaw, SHC (6). W. Cottam, fly (2) v. T. Littlefair, AR (7). C. Mitchell, Ry (5) v. P. Bladen, LW (6). H, France, R. (4) v. J. Jones, CA (4).</p>
        <p>E. Harper,„ CA (3) v. W. Dutton, Ry (6). Pritchard. C (6) v. A. Jones,, LW (7). W. Caddick, B (4) v. B. Forster, R (5). W. Starkey, SHE (5) v. J. Gleave, By (1). W. Westen, AA (3) v. W. Prichard, 3111 (6). R. Looker, WR (4) v. W. Budge. CA (4). E. Clare, LW (2) v. W. Daniels, By (1). J. Caddick, 3111 (6) v. J. Pollard, II &amp; K (6).</p>
        <p>4.30. F. Howard, N (6) v. L. Day, WX (7). W. Pilkerton, R (6) v. S. Keen, G (7). J. Wilkinson, WE (5) v. W. Spruce, P &amp; K (7). W. Charnock, R (6), bye. H. Nicholls, P &amp; K (7) v. J. Bartley, LW (5). W. Thomason, MH (2) v. T. Moores, FM (6). J. Goulding, SHC (6) v. F. Brandwood, PK (7). R. Knight, fun., Ry (5) v. J. Willett, C (6).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0168" n="art0168">
        <head>4.55.</head>
        <p>4.55.</p>
        <p>B. Pearnley, LW (7) V. J. Holloway, PK (7). J. Grounds, P &amp;K (7) V. R. Barnett, P &amp; K (5). A. Lester, MH (7) v. H. Shaw, SHC (6). J. Darbyshire, By (5) V. A. Hackett, P &amp; (5). W. Ashbrooke, CL (5) v. J. Eaves, P &amp; K (5). W. Blackledge, P &amp; K (3) V. J. Jolley, WC (sc.) I'. Wright, T &amp; G (5) v. J. Kirkhain, PK (6). A. 'Warburton, WX (1) v. J. Jeavons, WE (6). Referee, W. Taylor.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0169" n="art0169">
        <head>LIBERAL ASSOCIATION.</head>
        <p>LIBERAL ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>U. Shaw's Great Success.</p>
        <p>Mr, George Shaw, of Fairfield Ward, won the premier prize given by .Councillor H. Roberts in the annual handicap, the final stages of which were played off on Saturday. There was much enthusiasm, and the play was of a very good quality, the winner displaying much skill with the woods. The prizes will he. Pre- sented in the New Memorial Hall at an early \date. The following are the details of the day's play :</p>
        <p>Abbreviations.—W, Whitecross; L, Latchford; St. A, St. Austin's; F, Fairfield; St. J, St. John's; B, Bewsey, TH, Town Hall; 0, Orford; H, Howley. First Round.—J. Knox, W, 3; W. Elwell, St. A, 4; J/Hill, L, 5; J. Barlow, St. A, ser.; J. Perry, F, 2; R. Colley, 3; M. Cunningham, 0,4; F. Dale, St. J, owes 1; H. Broadhurst, F, 4; A. Dennett, St. A, 2; W. Crawford, B, 2; A. Broadhurst, W, owes 1; W. Bouchier, B, 5; P. Taylor, W, 3; R. Deakin, W, 3; J. Archer, TH, 3; W. Locker, W, 3; A. Payne, St. A, 3; W. Timmins, W, 4; J. Davies, L' 1; G. Shaw, F, 2; J. Ashburner, St. J, 3; J. Lawless, W, 3; T. Welsby, W, 2; D. Stokes, Tll, 2; T. Moores, St. A, 5; J. Wood, TH, 1; T. Badger, St. A, 4; J. Wood, St. A, scr.; H. Kynaston, W, 4; E. Massey, B, 6; B. Fogg, 0,2; R Jennings, 0,3; R. Jefferson, St. A, scr.; H. Benion, St. A. 2; J. Moss, St. A, 3; N. Cook, L, 3; W. Jones, W, scr.; E. Wilcox, W, 1; W. Morgan, H, 3; E. Baker, St. A, 3; A. Forster, St. A, 4; W. Buck- ley, W, 4; M. Llewellyn, H, 3; I'. Wright, W, scr.; T. Massey, 0,5; T. Williams, St. A, 4; H. Waywell, 0,5; J. Woodward, St. A, 3; J. Gibson, TH, 2; D. Beswick, W, 5; J. Graham, St. .A, 2; F. Molyneux, 0,3; E. Warburton, St. J, 3; W. Princep, W, 5; E. Appleby, W, 3; F: Grey, W, 2; W. Corlett, W, 2; T. Harrington, 0, S;A. Lingard, L, 3; A. Webb, W, scr.; M. Brookes, W, 3; T. Pownall, W, 5; W. Farring- ton, W, 4.</p>
        <p>Second Round.—J. Knox, J. irin, J. Perry, F. Dale, H. Broadhurst, W. Crawford, W. ,Bou- elder, R. Deakin, J. Davies, G. Shaw, D. Stokes, J. Wood, Welsby, D. Stokes, T. Badger, J. Wood, E. Massey, B. Jennings, H. Benion, N. Cook, W. Morgan, E. Baker, W. Buckley, P. Wright, T. Williams, J. Woodward, J. Graham, F. Moly- neux, W. Princep, F. Grey, T. Harrington, M. Brooks, W. Farrington. Third Round.—J. Hill, r. Dale, Ti. Broad- hurst, E. Deakip, J. Davies, G. Shaw, D. Stokes, J. Wood, H. Benion, W. Morgan, E. Baker, T. Williams, J. Graham, F. Molyneux, T. Harring- ton, M. Brookes. Fourth Round.—J. Hill, H. Broadhurst, G. Shaw, J. Wood, W. Morgan, E. Baker, F. Moly- neux, M. Brookes.</p>
        <p>Fifth Round.-11, Broadhurst, G. Shaw, W. Morgan, F. Molyneux. Semi-final.—G. Shaw, F. Xiolyneux. Final.—G. Shaw.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0170" n="art0170">
        <head>ODDFELLOU S.</head>
        <p>THE ODDFELLOU S.</p>
        <p>• Handicap for "Sir Gilbert Greeitall " Challenge Cup.</p>
        <p>The above handicap in connection with the Warrington district was commenced on Satur- day on the Bull's Head Hotel Green, Church. street. During the afternoon some very good games were played and the green was in splen- did order. Owing to the rain it was impossible to get beyond the fourth round, and the com- mittee decided that the semi-final and final should be played on August Monday morning, but the rain again came and prevented any play that morning, and such games were accordingly postponed Intil Thursday evening. On Thursday evening the handicap was com- pleted, the closing game between James A. Melbourne and W. Daniels being very keenly contested. At the ninth end Daniels was lead- ing 10-4, but Melbourne eventually recovered himself and scored four in the last three ends, and won by 13-12. The Grand Master of the district (Bro. Harry Lawrence) formally presented the cup to the winner, who is a member of the " William Savage '! Lodge, and in so doing stated that he was pleased to present the cup to that Lodge, that being the first occasion on which one of their members had won it. Bro. Melbourne returned thanks. The Grand Master also thanked the host (F.F.G.M. George F. Freeman) for having placed his green at the committee's disposal for the handicap and for his kindness throughout the same. _ _</p>
        <p>The remaining prizes will be distributed to the winners at the Bull's Head Hotel at an early, date, due notice of which will be for- warded to the different Lodge Secretaries in the district. The following are the winners in the various rounds:— Preliminary Round.—John Carter, C, 4; Wm. Eyes, PW, scr.,• Arthur Clare, T, 1; Thomas J. Rigby, C, 3; J. W. Rigby, C, 2; W. Leigh, Latchford, C, 4; Arthur Ince, HR 3; Harry Langley, PW, 1; John Ault, PW, 2; A. Duck- worth, PW, 4; George F. Freeman, PW, scr.; William T. Eccles, PW, 5; Simeon Monks, HR,. 5; James Massey, WS, 4; William Bibby, AN, 3; W. Robinson, C, 3; N.J. Clarke, C, 2. • First Round.—Ed. Lawrence, PW, 4; W. It9b- inson, C, 3; John Wilson, T, 3; James A. Mel- bourne, WS, 2; William E. Clare, HR, 5; Walter Langley, PW, 1; S. Williams, C, George Highain, WS, 6; David Ellison, jun., C, 6; George Owen, T, 3; D. Ferguson,. PW, 3; Thomas J. Rigby, C, 3; Henry Jones, T, 5; W. Daniels, PW, owes 1; Hy. Langley, PW, 1; Thomas 'E. Worthington, PW, 6; Elijah Lunt (No. 1), PW, 3; John Ault, PW, 2; W. Andrews, PW, owes 1; Edward Lunt, PW, 3; William Eyes, PW, scr.; George F. Freeman, PW, ser.; J. Wrench, PW, 2; Samuel Wray, C, 3; M. Wil- cock, PW, 3; Arthur Clare, T, 1; Fred Lawless, C, 3; Elijah Lunt (No. 2), PW, 2; Arthur Pen- nington, C, 5; John Daintith, C, 6; : James Leah, T, 2; R. Eyes, PW, 3. Second Round.—D. Ferguson, James Leah, Samuel Wray, John Ault, William Eyes, Wm. E. Clare, George Owen, W. Andrews, S. Wil- liams, W. Daniels, Arthur Clare, James A. Melbourne, Hy. Langley, Thomas J. Rigby, David Ellison, jun., John Daintith. Third Round.—William Eyes, John Daintith, Arthur Clare, George Owen, James A. Mel- bourne, W. Andrews, David Ferguson, W. Daniels. Fourth Round.—W. Daniels, James A. Mel- bourne, William Eyes, George Owen. Semi-final.—W. Daniels, James A. Melbourne. Final.--Janles A. Melbourne.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0171" n="art0171">
        <head>ATHLETIC CLUB SPORTS.</head>
        <p>ATHLETIC CLUB SPORTS.</p>
        <p>A Successful Function on the Football</p>
        <p>Ground.</p>
        <p>The second annual sports of the Warrington Athletic Club were held on the Football Ground at Wilderspool on Bank Holiday, and they at- tracted a good crowd. Some good running was witnessed, and every event produced some inter- esting feature. The results were as follows :- 100 Yards Flat Race Handicap (open).—Heat- winners: J. Spencer, Warrington A.C.; J. Flet- cher, Waterloo H.; W. E. Bunting, Manchester A.C.; G. Baines, Manchester A.C.; R. Webster, Liverpool; H. Smith, Leigh H.; T. Dennett, Warrington A.C.; T. H. Scott, Wirral A.C.; S. Green, Salford H. Final: 1, G. Baines; 2, S. Green; 3, W. E. Bunting. 150 Yards Flat Race (scholars).—Heat-Win- ners: R. H. Watson, Arpley-street, 13 years 11 months; E. Bit•chall, Parochial, 12 years 1 month; J. P. Clarke, St. Alban's, 12 years 5 months; W. Downes, Beamont, 13 years 1 month; A. Caldwell, St. Thomas', 11 years; J. T. Monks, Parochial, 13 years 4 months; E. Makin, Beamont, 12 years 7 months. Final: 1, J. T. Monks; 2, E. Makin; 3, R. H. Watson. One Mile Flat Race Handicap (open).-1, C. Davies, Waterloo H.; 2, S. Sherlock, Bolton M.H. ; 3, J. McCoy, St. Helens Recs. 220 Yards Flat Race Handicap (open).—Heat- winners: J. Fletcher, Waterloo H.; E. F. Con- cannon, Knotty Ash H.; M. L. Jones, Liverpool H. and A.C.; S. Siddall, Wr rington. A.C.; J. Whitlow. Runcorn; D. McAl ese, Conliffe H.; G. Baines, Manchester A.C.; 1 . Yates, Leigh F. H. Final: 1, •F. Yates; 2, M. L. Jones; 3, E Concannon. One Mile Novice Cycle Race Handicap.—Heat- winners: D. Walker, Salford A.C.; R. Lawrence, Manchester; G. 11. Burden, Warrington A.C.; T. McEwen, Geisha W. Final: 1, R. Lawrence; 2, T. McEwen ; 3, D. Walker. 60 Yards Sack Race (scholars).—Heat winners: S. R. Lodge, A. Dover, A. Livesey, Archie George, R. H. Watson. Final: 1, R. H. Watson; 2, A. Livesey. Half-mile Flat Race (open).-1, J. W. Watson, Warrington A.C.; 2, R. Baldwin, Leigh H.; 3, W. Bolton, Warrington A.C. Two Miles Junior Team Race.—lndividual winner: Atkins (Hallamshire H.). Winning team: 1, Hallamshire H., viz.: Atkins, Oates and Anderson; 2, Manchester A.C.,. viz.: S. Atkinson, A. Hawes and F. C. Pepworth. One of the chief attractions was a 9st. 41b. boxing contest, in which there were eight com- petitors.. The winner was J. Lyall, Hulme, who beat John Smith, of Liverpool, on points in the final. Smith took second prize. A special exhibition of boxing was given by Sergeant-Instructor W. A. Rice (Army and Navy light-weight champion) and Sergeant-In- structor Smith.</p>
        <p>Interesting physical and gymnastic displays were given by the boys of Farnworth Nautical School, whose band played selections during the afternoon. _ _</p>
        <p>The prizes were distributed by Mrs. Ej Osborne, who was thanked on the motion of Mr. A. Bailie.</p>
        <p>LIST OF OFFICIALS.</p>
        <p>The officials were as follows: Referee, Mr. F. Latham, N.C.A.A.; 'judges, Councillor E. Osborne, Messrs. H. Ashton, T. Astill, H. Hope; stewards, Messrs, A. Bailie (chief), H. Arm- strong, S. Andrews, J. Bluck, T. Barnes. J. Berry, G. Evans, T. W. Evans. .T. Moorfield, J. Riley, W. Whittle, J. Walker, J. Battersby, and Club Committee; starter, Mr. A. E. Hayman. Boxing 'competition officials: Referee, Mr. R. Beaman; judges, Mr. A. Regan, Sergeant-In- structor Smith; time-keeper, Mr. H. Beaman; committee‘ Messrs. T. Roberts (chairman), T. Whalley, 3. Tavlin, E. Tavlin, Matt. Tavlin, J. Durham. W. Monks, 3. Bate; finance stewards, Messrs. F. Mumby (chief). IL James. W. James, G. IT. .Anderton; hon, secretary and treasurer, Mr. Reuben Bennett; hon. assistant secretary, Mr. W. W. Taylor.</p>
