      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0183" n="art0183">
        <head>TIIE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, AUGUST 8, 1914.</head>
        <p>TIIE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, AUGUST 8, 1914.</p>
        <p>puted that something like 200 animals have already been removed from Warrington and dis- trict.</p>
        <p>The farmers in the immediate locality have also suffered. According to the story of one, he haa-lost five of his best horses, and was in a dilemma as to how he was to work his farm, more particularly as the harvest was coming on.</p>
        <p>The feeling in Warrington yesterday was that if more horses were commandeered it would prove a serious matter, as food stuffs could not he delivered. Some of the principal merchants have approached the Mayor in the hope that he can use Some influence in retaining the horses, so that food might be distributed as speedily as possible.</p>
