        <p>assumption is that the drays are for food distri- bution, but to settle this point we must "wait and see." HORSES COMMANDEERED. A large number of horses in Lancashire and Cheshire have been taken over for Army pur- poses, and several firms in Warrington have had an experience of this. It has been roughly corn-</p>
        <p>circumstances. It would mean a great induce- ment for people to store up beer, &amp;c., in their homes, and the supposed remedy would be worse than the suggested evil. Of course, it is not for me to decide, and the Licensing Committee have no powers to enforce it." PRINCE OF WALES TO THE MAYOR. The Mayor, last evening, received the follow- ing telegram from the Prince of Wales : Earnestly trust that you will assist my national relief fund by opening subscription list without delay and forwarding results to Buckingham Palace. Please do all that lies in your power to in- terest those amongst whom your interest extends.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON, RUNCOIRN AND DISTRICT SAVINGS RANK. The Trustees have received a communication from the National Debt Commissioners to the effect that : • Should the conditions at present obtaining tend towards an exceptional withdrawal of deposits from the Savings Bank, they will be prepared to supply it with as much money as may be required to meet all demands. The National Debt Commissioners add that mature consideration will doubtless convince the depositors that the safety of their deposits is amply secured. The depositors may rest assured that their position is perfectly secure, and they are advised, in their own as well as the National, interests, not to withdraw more than is neces- sary for their immediate requirements. The Great Western Railway Company give notice that the issue of tourist, excursion, week- end, Saturday to Monday, market, pleasure party, and all other descriptions of tickets at reduced fares (except workmen's) are suspended forthwith and until further notice. The wholesale prices of Hartley's Jams and Marmalade are not increased.</p>
